---
/**
 * Standalone Index contribution control.
 *
 * A separate processing path from the follow-up form, and it must stay
 * that way. It never sits inside the follow-up form and it sends no
 * identity field of any kind: ten answer values and two version
 * strings, nothing else.
 *
 * It sends the answers raw rather than bucketed. Bucketing would mean
 * shipping ordinal values to the browser, which is precisely what must
 * not happen. Since the question set no longer asks for sector, size or
 * role, the payload carries no organisational detail at all.
 *
 * WHAT THIS CANNOT CLAIM YET. Submissions relay through Formspree to a
 * mailbox, so a contribution and a later follow-up arrive in the same
 * inbox and the operator could correlate them by timestamp. The strong
 * unlinkability the plan describes needs the Worker, a buffered write
 * and a separate database. The consent copy says what this does, not
 * what Phase 3 will do.
 */
---

<section class="benchmark" data-benchmark hidden aria-labelledby="benchmark-heading">
  <div class="wrap-narrow">
    <div class="benchmark-inner">
      <h3 class="h3" id="benchmark-heading">Contribute to the Intervention Readiness Index.</h3>

      <p class="body-sm muted benchmark-intro">
        Intervene is building the first dataset of how organisations actually
        answer these questions. Contributing takes one click and asks for
        nothing further.
      </p>

      <label class="consent-check">
        <input type="checkbox" data-benchmark-consent />
        <span class="choice-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="consent-check-text">
          Include my ten answers in the Intervention Readiness Index. The
          contribution is sent on its own and carries no name, email address,
          organisation or role.
        </span>
      </label>

      <div class="benchmark-actions">
        <button type="button" class="btn-ghost" data-benchmark-submit>
          Contribute my answers
        </button>
        <p class="body-sm benchmark-note">
          What the Index holds is set out in the
          <a href="/legal/privacy/" class="link">privacy notice</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="field-error benchmark-error" data-benchmark-error role="alert" hidden></p>

      <p class="benchmark-confirmed" data-benchmark-confirmed tabindex="-1" hidden>
        Recorded, and thank you. Your answers were sent without a name, an email
        address, an organisation or a role attached.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .benchmark {
    padding: 48px 0 96px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hair);
  }
  .benchmark-inner { max-width: 62ch; }
  .benchmark-intro { margin: 16px 0 28px; }

  .benchmark-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 20px;
    margin-top: 28px;
  }
  .benchmark-note {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--faint);
    max-width: 40ch;
  }

  .benchmark-confirmed {
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    border: 1px solid var(--accent);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .benchmark-confirmed:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  @media print {
    .benchmark { display: none; }
  }
</style>
